---
layout: compress
swcache: true
---

{%- comment -%}
  Overrides the theme's search index (gem: assets/js/data/search.json).

  The theme indexes the whole rendered post, so every fenced code block ends up
  in the index. On this blog that is 47% of the markdown: it doubles the payload
  the browser downloads before the first search, and it makes queries match YAML
  keys, log dumps and terminal output instead of prose.

  Here the <pre> blocks are dropped before the text is extracted. Inline <code>
  is kept, so a flag or command name mentioned in a sentence still matches. The
  rest of the pipeline mirrors the theme's `post-summary.html full_text=true`,
  minus its line-number workaround, which is unnecessary once <pre> is gone.
{%- endcomment -%}

[
  {% for post in site.posts %}
  {%- assign segments = post.content | split: '<pre' -%}
  {%- assign prose = segments[0] -%}
  {%- for segment in segments offset: 1 -%}
    {%- assign tail = segment | split: '</pre>' -%}
    {%- if tail.size > 1 -%}
      {%- assign prose = prose | append: tail[1] -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign prose = prose
    | markdownify
    | strip_html
    | newline_to_br
    | replace: '<br />', ' '
    | strip_newlines
    | strip
  -%}
  {
    "title": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ post.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
    "categories": {{ post.categories | join: ', ' | jsonify }},
    "tags": {{ post.tags | join: ', ' | jsonify }},
    "date": {{ post.date | jsonify }},
    "content": {{ prose | jsonify }}
  }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]
